%U A400909 43672797212584144531390464000,1807128421375029376606764016435200,100859380125598781229386573338312704000,7389880189255706071817086496369018083737600
%N A400909 Number of labeled loopless digraphs on 2n vertices such that deg^+(v) + deg^-(v) = 3 for every vertex v.
%C A400909 Here deg^+(v) and deg^-(v) denote the outdegree and indegree of v, respectively.
%C A400909 More generally, the number of labeled loopless digraphs on n vertices such that deg^+(v) + deg^-(v) = m for every vertex v is the coefficient of x_1^m*...*x_n^m in Product_{1 <= i < j <= n} (1 + x_i*x_j)^2.
%H A400909 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A400909/b400909.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..100</a>
%F A400909 a(n) = coefficient of x_1^3*...*x_(2n)^3 in Product_{1 <= i < j <= 2n} (1 + x_i*x_j)^2.
%e A400909 For n = 2, there are 2n = 4 vertices. There are 2^6 = 64 orientations of the complete graph K_4.
%e A400909 The other digraphs have two disjoint pairs of oppositely directed arcs and two single arcs joining the pairs. There are 3 choices for the pairing, 2 choices for the matching between the pairs, and 2^2 orientations of the single arcs.
%e A400909 Thus a(2) = 64 + 3*2*2^2 = 88.
%Y A400909 Cf. A400907 (total degree 2).
%K A400909 nonn,new
%O A400909 0,3
